TTYCHATTER.BASH(1)          User Commands          TTYCHATTER.BASH(1)

NAME
    ttychatter.bash - dependency-light Bash-only terminal client

SYNOPSIS
    ttychatter.bash [session]
    ttychatter.bash --resume <session|session.log|/path/session.log>
    ttychatter.bash --models [--model-type TYPE]
    ttychatter.bash --routers
    ttychatter.bash --update-models
    ttychatter.bash --test-model <model_id>
    ttychatter.bash --select-model
    ttychatter.bash --doctor
    ttychatter.bash --demo
    ttychatter.bash --version
    ttychatter.bash --loopback
    ttychatter.bash --loopback-file <path>
    ttychatter.bash --help

DESCRIPTION
    ttychatter.bash is the Bash-only edition of ttychatter. It avoids Python and
    remains dependency-light while still providing an end-user interactive chat
    client with sessions, model tools, memory, logs, and attachment attempts.

ROUTERS AND FIXED MODELS
    The Bash-only edition can filter model-list output by OpenRouter type:

        ttychatter.bash --routers
        ttychatter.bash --models --model-type routers
        ttychatter.bash --models --model-type fixed
        ttychatter.bash --models --model-type free
        ttychatter.bash --models --model-type auto

    Without jq, model metadata parsing is best-effort. The client remains
    usable because exact model IDs can still be entered and tested.

RUNTIME COMMAND MODE
    Inputs beginning with ':' are local commands rather than messages to
    OpenRouter. Examples:
        :help
        :models
        :routers
        :select-model
        :test-model openrouter/auto
        :memory
        :attach ./notes.txt
        :credits
        :quit

LOOPBACK OUTPUT
    ttychatter.bash --loopback
        Sends interface text to stderr and clean AI responses to stdout so the
        output can be piped into another program.


MODEL FAVORITES
    Model favorites/bookmarks are stored as plain text and are shared with
    model-list sorting/filtering where the client supports it.

    Commands:
        ttychatter.bash --favorites
        ttychatter.bash --favorite-model <model_id>
        ttychatter.bash --unfavorite-model <model_id>

    Runtime commands inside chat:
        :favorites
        :favorite <model_id>
        :unfavorite <model_id>

DISPLAY AND SEND CONFIGURATION
    THEME controls the line-oriented display profile where meaningful.
    Supported values include default, dim, high_contrast, mono, and
    solarized_dark. Bash clients only emit ANSI styling when stdout is a
    terminal; loopback/pipeline output remains plain text.

    SEND_INPUT controls the interactive input loop.  ctrl_d keeps the classic
    multiline Bash behavior.  enter reads one line per message.  ctrl_enter is
    terminal-dependent and is not reliable in line-oriented Bash clients.

CODE BLOCK ATTACHMENT THRESHOLD
    CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES controls when generated fenced code blocks are
    saved as attachments.  Shorter blocks remain inline so ordinary short code
    examples do not disappear from the transcript.

VERSION
    ttychatter.bash version 0.12.0-bash-only
